      "created_at": "2017-03-30T12:43:40Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-03-30T12:43:40Z",
      "body": "Hello @kidburglar,\r\nthis is a tricky one :)\r\n\r\nOn one side I don't want to save the master password anywhere\r\nOn other side, I will improve the user experience to save master password\r\n\r\nThis is a security problem: usability versus security\r\n\r\nFor me your master password should always be in your head, and you should use only trusted devices.\r\n\r\nBut your issue make me think about an alternative:\r\nGenerate all passwords based on all your password profiles and store them in the session. \r\nLike this you can open the app, enter your master password one, and copy every password for one day for example.\r\n\r\nLet's continue the discussion here",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
